---
title: How a Delivery API read is authenticated and cached
---
flowchart LR
    accTitle: How a Delivery API read is authenticated and cached
    accDescr: A Delivery API GET at cdn.{domain} reaches the delivery Worker's uncached gateway, which first rate-limits the client IP to 1200 requests a minute ①. It then authenticates the CDA or CPA key on every request: the principal is read from KV_CACHE by the key's peppered hash, and only on a KV miss is the key looked up on a D1 read replica and the principal cached for up to 60 seconds under the principals tag for its space ②. A bad key or a rate-limited client gets a 401 or 429 that is never cached. The gateway reduces the principal to a visibility profile, a hash of space, key kind, sorted scopes and content grants, and forwards a canonical URL built from that profile, the path and the sorted query, with the principal in an internal header ③. Workers Caching in front of the Delivery entrypoint answers a hit with the body every reader of that profile shares ④; on a miss the entrypoint runs the delivery routes against a D1 read replica and returns a 200 with a strong ETag and the environment's cache-tag, which the cache stores ⑤. Back in the gateway, an If-None-Match that names the ETag gets a 304, and anything else gets the body ⑥.

    Consumer([Delivery API consumer]):::external

    subgraph Gateway["delivery gateway: uncached, publicly routed"]
        Limit{Under 1200 a minute for this IP?}
        Auth[authenticateCached]
        Profile[Visibility profile and canonical URL]:::focal
        Cond{If-None-Match names the ETag?}
    end

    subgraph Internal["Not routable from outside: trusts its principal header"]
        Cache[(Workers Caching, keyed by profile and URL)]:::focal
        DEnt[Delivery entrypoint routes]:::primary
    end

    KV[(KV_CACHE principal cache)]:::store
    D1R[(D1 read replica)]:::store
    Reject([401 or 429, never cached]):::external
    Answer([Response to the consumer]):::external

    Consumer -->|"GET /delivery/… with bearer key"| Limit
    Limit -->|"① no: rejects"| Reject
    Limit -->|yes: authenticates| Auth
    Auth -->|"② reads principal by key hash"| KV
    Auth -.->|on KV miss, looks up key| D1R
    Auth -->|rejects bad key| Reject
    Auth -->|passes principal| Profile
    Profile -->|"③ forwards canonical URL"| Cache
    Cache -->|"④ hit: returns shared body"| Cond
    Cache -->|"miss: invokes"| DEnt
    DEnt -->|"⑤ reads published content"| D1R
    DEnt -->|stores 200 with ETag and cache-tag| Cache
    Cond -->|"⑥ yes: answers 304"| Answer
    Cond -->|no: answers 200 with body| Answer

